From: Fix HDBSS DBM incorrectly applied to VFIO MMIO regions
Subject: [BUGFIX] Add !device check to prevent DBM for MMIO memory
Date: 2026-05-15

Bug Description:
HDBSS incorrectly adds DBM (Dirty Bit Modifier) to VFIO MMIO BAR regions,
causing device access issues and migration failures.

Root Cause:
In user_mem_abort(), the DBM setting logic (mmu.c:1682) does not check
if the fault is for device/MMIO memory. This causes:
1. VFIO MMIO BAR Stage-2 PTEs get DBM bit
2. HDBSS hardware attempts dirty tracking on MMIO regions
3. MMIO is not real memory, hardware behavior becomes undefined
4. Device state may become inconsistent
5. Migration verification fails on PCI config space hardware bits

Fix:
Add !device check before setting DBM, ensuring DBM is only used for
RAM memory, not for Device/MMIO memory.

Tested:
- Two-round VFIO migration with hisi_zip accelerator
- Before fix: Second migration fails with PCI config mismatch
- After fix: All migrations succeed

---

 arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c | 2 +- 
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
index xxx..xxx 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
@@ -1681,7 +1681,7 @@ static int user_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t fault_ipa,
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_HDBSS
-	if (kvm->enable_hdbss && logging_active)
+	if (!device && kvm->enable_hdbss && logging_active)
 		prot |= KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_DBM;
 #endif
 
---

Explanation:

The 'device' variable is set at line 1620:
    if (kvm_is_device_pfn(pfn)) {
        device = true;
    }

kvm_is_device_pfn() checks:
    return !pfn_is_map_memory(pfn);

VFIO MMIO BARs have PFNs that are NOT map memory (not in memblock),
so device=true for all VFIO MMIO regions.

DBM (Dirty Bit Modifier) is a hardware feature for tracking RAM dirty
pages. It should NEVER be used for MMIO regions because:
1. MMIO is device memory, not RAM
2. HDBSS hardware behavior for MMIO is undefined
3. MMIO writes are device operations, not memory modifications
4. Dirty tracking MMIO causes no benefit and potential harm

This fix ensures DBM is only applied when:
- !device: Memory is RAM (not MMIO)
- enable_hdbss: HDBSS feature is enabled
- logging_active: Dirty logging is active (migration)

